commit cd9ae7b6
author: cdvankammen
date: 2026-10-22 15:41:21 -0600
subject: fix(cloudflare-deploy): wrap subdomain-enable in try/catch + add regression tests

The subdomain-enable step already documented itself as non-fatal
("We don't fail completely here, just continue") but threw uncaught
errors on timeout/network failure. Wrapped in try/catch so a timed-out
or failed enable step does not abort the entire deploy.

Added 5-test vitest suite covering:
- All 3 Cloudflare fetch calls carry AbortSignal.timeout(30000)
- Upload timeout surfaces as 500 with timeout-flavored error
- Subdomain-enable timeout is non-fatal (deploy still succeeds)
- Subdomain-retrieval timeout yields a non-2xx response
- Missing credentials short-circuit before any fetch

Fixes GAP-P2-22.

